A||||3||Dan87GT||3.4 Crate Motor(12363230) - exhaust valves||||1||
Z||000000||Dan87GT||01-22-2000||08:02 AM||||What size exhaust valves do the 3.4 crate motors come with???, I have looked at several  links and some dealerships say 1.42 others say 1.60, the GM parts catalog says 1.42 Anybody checked???||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||01-22-2000||11:28 AM||||1.42 exhaust 1.72 intake||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||01-22-2000||12:28 PM||||There are rumors of a HO 3.4 cast iron head with 1.6" exhaust valves that was used in some Camaros, but nobody can seem to prove this. The GM HO 3.4 crate engine has the same heads as the Fiero, 1.72" intakes and 1.42" exhaust valves.||||reg||1
Z||000003||cobra427||01-22-2000||10:00 PM||||Here is the info that I have from the GM Performance catalog (2000) as reguards the 60* v-6 cylinder heads.  It is as follows:<BR>1.-Standard cast iron heads pt#14054884<BR>   valve size-1.60in.x1.30ex<BR>2.-H/O cast iron heads,same part # except with larger valve size-1.72"in.x1.42"ex.<BR>3.-Production "Generation ll" aluminum heads.<BR>   pt.#10048649.These have the splayed valves<BR>   for better breathing.Machined for the  <BR>   1.72"in.x1.42"ex. valves.<BR>4.-Part# 10218168 is the "Generation lll" <BR>   cast iron heads. Used in late model 60* <BR>   v-6's.They feature an increase of <BR>   0.040" in intake valve diameter and a <BR>   reshaped port for a flow improvement of<BR>   16.7% at 0.450" of valve lift. The exhaust<BR>   port has been reshaped into a "D" port<BR>   configuration for a flow improvement of<BR>   31.7% at 0.450" of valve lift.<BR>It would appear to me that,if my math is correct, that the biggest factory heads are the Gen lll cast iron heads with the 1.76"<BR>intake valves and standard 1.42" exhaust valves.  Looks like a better head,BUT, will <BR>they fit?  I don't know. I just report the news,I don't make it.   Hope this has helped somebody.||||reg||1
